From 9ae6e3f368907f9fbf6a57421dce23b10191318f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DByte308 <69403407+DByte308@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:00:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/28] d/pimax_p3c: fix stereo, add eye tracking and
 gaze-steered quad views

Stereo (Crystal Super Ultrawide, verified in the headset):
- view_fov(): use the visible extent around the lens centre per side; the old
  signed fov_fix_degree plus the per-eye side swap gave the right eye the left
  eye's frustum, and the cant was applied twice (pose and frustum).
- lens centre from lens.separation + level offset (~2 mm nasal) instead of
  h_size/2. Override: PIMAX_LENS_SEP_MM.
- diagnostics: PIMAX_CANT_SCALE (percent), PIMAX_BLANK_EYE=0|1.

Eye tracking: Tobii VR4 EyeChip over libusb (TTP), XRT_DEVICE_EYE_GAZE_INTERACTION
device, per-eye fallback; native quad views (views 2-3 follow gaze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
